---
title: "attendances_table_rls (0001_create_attendance_schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_create: CREATE TABLE attendance.attendances (id UUID PK, user_id UUID FK, card_id, type, timestamp, date, created_at)
    q_create --> q_enable_rls: ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY
    q_enable_rls --> q_create_idx1: CREATE INDEX idx_attendances_date_user (date, user_id)
    q_create_idx1 --> q_create_idx2: CREATE INDEX idx_attendances_user_timestamp (user_id, timestamp)
    q_create_idx2 --> q_policy_service: CREATE POLICY service_role ALL using(true) with check(true)
    q_policy_service --> q_policy_auth: CREATE POLICY authenticated SELECT using(auth.uid() = user_id)
    q_policy_auth --> [*]: table ready

    note right of q_enable_rls
        INV-001: RLS is enabled on attendance.attendances
        INV-002: service_role has unrestricted access
        INV-003: authenticated users can only SELECT their own records (auth.uid() = user_id)
        INV-004: No INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE policy for authenticated users (writes go through SECURITY DEFINER RPC)
        INV-005: type column has no CHECK constraint (unlike public.attendances which constrains to 'in'/'out')
        INV-006: user_id FK cascades delete from attendance.users
    end note
